# Native server-side 301s, served by Cloudflare Pages (evaluated before static
# assets, so they take precedence over the built meta-refresh redirect pages —
# turning those client-side stubs into real 301s, better for SEO and speed).
#
# The astro `redirects` config in astro.config.mjs is deliberately KEPT: it emits
# the meta-refresh HTML fallback so these paths still redirect on the GitHub Pages
# origin BEFORE the DNS cutover to Cloudflare Pages (GH Pages ignores _redirects).
# Post-cutover the HTML is shadowed by the 301s below and is harmless.
/about                   /  301
/about/                  /  301
/resume                  /  301
/underconstruction       /  301
/underconstruction.html  /  301

# Slug renamed quantum-protein-kernel → quantum-ml-classifier, whose demo then
# moved under the AI/ML umbrella. Enumerated exact paths (no splat, no chains):
# the detail page anchors to the timeline card, the /app deep link lands on the
# umbrella demo.
/projects/quantum-protein-kernel        /#quantum-ml-classifier  301
/projects/quantum-protein-kernel/       /#quantum-ml-classifier  301
/projects/quantum-protein-kernel/app    /projects/ai-ml/app/  301
/projects/quantum-protein-kernel/app/   /projects/ai-ml/app/  301

